From: linux_lenovod330
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: add standalone backlight-enable GPIO toggle (D330)
License: SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only (derivative of intel_dsi_vbt.c,
         matching the license of the file it patches, regardless of this
         repo's overall license)

Adds a write-only module parameter, d330_backlight_gpio, that directly
drives VBT GPIO index 4 (the panel's backlight-enable line) via the
driver's existing bxt_gpio_set_value(), completely decoupled from the
CRTC enable/disable state machine.

Rationale: on Gemini-Lake-class DSI panels wired like the Lenovo
D330-10IGM, the backlight-enable GPIO (index 4) is circuit-independent
of the panel power rail (index 3) -- confirmed against the board
schematic. The known "black screen after suspend/DPMS" bug on this
panel family is triggered by the panel power/reset GPIO cycle and DSI
protocol re-init that happen on every CRTC disable/enable, not by the
backlight line itself. This lets userspace turn the backlight fully
off/on (e.g. on an idle timer, or on lid close/open) without ever
going near that path.

GPIO index 3 (panel power) and index 4 (backlight) are already held
exclusively by i915 as gpiod consumers from probe time onward (visible
in `gpioinfo` as `[used]`, consumer being the i915 PCI device), so this
cannot be done from userspace with generic gpiod/libgpiod tools -- it
has to be driven from inside the module.

The connector pointer is captured in intel_dsi_vbt_gpio_init(), which
always runs exactly once during intel_dsi_init() regardless of
platform (its body is a no-op outside VLV/CHV, but it still runs) and
regardless of whether the panel came up via a full VBT sequence or via
i915's BIOS-fb "fastset" reuse path -- so the pointer is valid before
any real DSI enable/disable cycle has ever executed.

See the accompanying README for background, verification notes, and
how to adapt the "4" (backlight GPIO index) if your panel uses a
different one.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dsi_vbt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dsi_vbt.c
@@ -315,6 +315,43 @@
 	soc_gpio_set_value(connector, gpio_index, NULL, gpio_index, value);
 }

+/*
+ * D330: standalone backlight-enable GPIO (VBT index 4) toggle, decoupled
+ * from the normal CRTC enable/disable state machine. The panel power rail
+ * (index 3) and DSI protocol re-init are never touched by this, so it does
+ * not go through the resume path that has the known black-screen bug (see
+ * the project README: backlight EN is circuit-independent of panel power
+ * per the board schematic). Captured connector pointer comes from
+ * intel_dsi_vbt_gpio_init(), which always runs once at probe regardless of
+ * platform or fastset.
+ */
+static struct intel_connector *d330_bl_connector;
+
+static int d330_backlight_gpio_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	unsigned long value;
+	int ret = kstrtoul(val, 0, &value);
+
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (!d330_bl_connector) {
+		pr_warn("d330_backlight_gpio: no connector captured yet\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
+	bxt_gpio_set_value(d330_bl_connector, 4, !!value);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct kernel_param_ops d330_backlight_gpio_ops = {
+	.set = d330_backlight_gpio_set,
+	.get = NULL,
+};
+module_param_cb(d330_backlight_gpio, &d330_backlight_gpio_ops, NULL, 0200);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(d330_backlight_gpio,
+		 "D330: directly drive VBT GPIO index 4 (backlight enable) without touching panel power/reset (write 0 or 1)");
+
 enum {
 	MIPI_RESET_1 = 0,
 	MIPI_AVDD_EN_1,
@@ -898,6 +935,8 @@
 	struct intel_display *display = to_intel_display(&intel_dsi->base);
 	struct intel_connector *connector = intel_dsi->attached_connector;
 	struct mipi_config *mipi_config = connector->panel.vbt.dsi.config;
+
+	d330_bl_connector = connector;
 	enum gpiod_flags flags = panel_is_on ? GPIOD_OUT_HIGH : GPIOD_OUT_LOW;
 	struct gpiod_lookup_table *gpiod_lookup_table = NULL;
 	bool want_backlight_gpio = false;
